        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Ran this branch locally. `local_cmd` is scoped to the `root_dir` block, so the second `validate_tsc_version(local_cmd)` gets nil. In a project with no `node_modules/.bin/tsc` but `tsc` on `$PATH`:\n\n```\nvim/_core/system:318: bad argument #1 to 'spawn' (string expected, got nil)\n```\n\nand nothing attaches.\n\nTwo smaller things. `cmd:match('tsc$')` checks `cmd`, which is still the `'tsc'` default at that point, not `bin` — so it's true on every iteration and the tsgo/tsc distinction doesn't hold. And `break` on a failed version check leaves the loop entirely instead of trying the next candidate, so `cmd` stays plain `'tsc'`; if that one is also pre-7.0 you're back where you started.\n\nI hit the same bug and opened #4505 — it probes in `root_dir` instead, caching the result per project root, so the check runs once per root and `cmd` can't end up with a binary `root_dir` didn't accept. Happy to close mine if you'd rather carry the fix here, just didn't want two PRs on the same file with no pointer between them.",
